      <h2 class="sec-headline">Three Leaders Lost — Who's in Charge?</h2>
      <p class="sec-lead">Between July 2024 and October 2024, Hamas lost three consecutive leaders: Ismail Haniyeh (assassinated in Tehran, July 31), then Yahya Sinwar (killed by IDF in Rafah, October 16). A five-member interim leadership council has governed the organization since. As of May–June 2026, Hamas completed internal elections selecting regional leaders and is finalizing selection of a new political bureau chief.</p>

